Mark the early boot functions

The kernel reaches the early boot phase and does not get past it,
and the last of the phase's own prints is on the screen while
bsd_init's are not.  The phase is a list of startup entries, and
this patch puts a number on each of the functions in it:

    01 source_pthread_bootstrap      07 vm_pageout_create_gc_thread
    02 telemetry_init               08 vm_deferred_reclamation_init
    03 set_awl_scratch...           09 personas_bootstrap
    04 iotrace_init                 10 cs_text_fixup_init
    05 pgz_init                     11 kcov_init
    06 kmem_crypto_init

The numbers are two digits because the panel is read from a
photograph of a phone that is held by hand.  They are also two
digits because the space is what they compete for: the console
blob needs 9518 bytes of the tail padding of __TEXT_EXEC and a
kernel with nothing in it has 9648, so every marker has to fit
in 130 bytes.

---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/source_pthread_bootstrap.c b/bsd/kern/source_pthread_bootstrap.c
index 40427eb..6f08d76 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/source_pthread_bootstrap.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/source_pthread_bootstrap.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ SECURITY_READ_ONLY_LATE(kern_return_t) source_pthread_status = KERN_FAILURE;
 static void
 source_pthread_bootstrap(void)
 {
+	printf("nio: %u\n", 1);
 	static kmod_info_t info = {
 		.info_version = KMOD_INFO_VERSION,
 		.name = "source-libpthread",
